    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "n300",
      "x": 1040,
      "y": 2880,
      "name": "note_493_flow",
      "width": 520,
      "height": 560,
      "content": "#493 Windows in-app updates — flow\n\n1. Check (unchanged): startup + every 6 h, own channel only (stable or nightly-win).\n2. Installable = newest Runner-Setup-*.exe with a .sig asset beside it. No .sig → notify-only: same dialog, View downloads only.\n3. Automatically download updates (default on) → download in the background to <app data>\\updates\\*.partial, verify the minisign signature with the compiled-in public key, rename → READY.\n4. ONE centered update dialog (cmp/UpdateDialog) over the 60% scrim is the whole UI. The sidebar icon and the Update button in Settings → Updates open the same dialog in the same state.\n5. Five user-facing states: Up to date, Available, Downloading, Ready, Failed. Checking is the idle button spinning; verifying is the tail of the bar; the failure reason is a message; \"installing\" is the app quitting.\n6. Progress lives only in the dialog. The Settings row shows a one-line status and never a bar.\n7. Install and restart is inside the Ready dialog. No separate confirm, no running-work warning: quitting stamps sessions for auto-resume as it does today.\n8. Confirm → spawn installer detached (/SILENT /NORESTART /WAITPID=<pid> /RELAUNCH=1 /LOG=…), then the normal quit path stamps sessions for auto-resume and stops PTYs. Installer waits for the pid, installs, relaunches Runner; on failure it relaunches the OLD Runner.\n\nDecisions\n- No auto-install ever; the dialog's button is the only gate.\n- Trust = minisign (Ed25519) sig from CI, independent of Authenticode (#497).\n- macOS untouched: Sparkle draws its own UI.\n\nSpec: docs/features/493-windows-auto-update.md"
    },
